{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities","id":1544449,"title":"Abilities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-10-22T01:24:42-07:00","id":1544449,"title":"Abilities","content":"How do you raise your abilities with magic mechanically? What spheres (not lower the difficulty but increase the dots)?<br /> For example if i wanted to download kung-fu like in the matrix. How can that be done?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T03:15:19-07:00","id":1544450,"title":"","content":"The game has largely avoided it through magic. Dream/Hypercram are the default ways of doing so... though there's no particular reason you couldn't use magic to increase the Background (either as an excuse to raise it, or to gain it temporarily).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T15:31:37-07:00","id":1544509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities#post1544449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How do you raise your abilities with magic mechanically? What spheres (not lower the difficulty but increase the dots)? For example if i wanted to download kung-fu like in the matrix. How can that be done?</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me link your question with what Heavy Arms wrote:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544450#post1544450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The game has largely avoided it through magic. Dream/Hypercram are the default ways of doing so... though there's no particular reason you couldn't use magic to increase the Background (either as an excuse to raise it, or to gain it temporarily).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, that is very true, the game always avoided to answer this. It seems, however, pretty easy to answer.<br /> <br /> Dream/Hypercram is background... What does it do thou? It gives access to knowledge you yourself don't have.<br /> <br /> Taking in consideration however that &quot;Walk on Dreams&quot; is a Mind 3 effect...<br /> <br /> I have created my own ways to answer that question a long time ago. So let's see:<br /> <br /> 1 - Copy the skill from someone who knows it: Mind 3 + Mind 1. With that effect you simply &quot;borrow&quot; the skill from someone who's better at it than you. It's a process similar to Mind Reading - in essence, that's what you're doing, you're mind reading someone while also applying Mind 1 on yourself to improve your own mind (but since Mind 1 is already contained on Mind 3, you don't need to specify it.<br /> <br /> Now, this is all well and good, but the problem is that you need that one person skilled to borrow the ability from, and you can't storage said knowledge. Unless...<br /> <br /> 2 - Storaging Knowledge: Mind 3 + Prime (lvl variable). Do you want to storage the skills you stole? Oops, forgive me, BORROWED. That's better.<br /> <br /> Well, look no further! You can create pendrive (or &quot;brainchips&quot;) to storage your huge collection of skills! (Or mystic tablet stones, or knowledge crystals, whatever).<br /> <br /> You are, essentially, creating a Magic Item that stores information easily turned into &quot;brain skills!.<br /> <br /> The reason why the lvl of Prime is variable is because it depends on having or not... Damn, I forgot what the word in English is... &quot;Solid Quintessence&quot;, you know what I mean - of the proper resonance. If you have that, Prime 2 can create one use only cheap chips, otherwise it requires Prime 3, and with the &quot;quint thing&quot; with proper resonance, Prime 3 can create a permanent one, otherwise it's Prime 4.<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T15:42:47-07:00","id":1544510,"title":"","content":"But wait! There's more! <br /> <br /> 3 - I have the Powaaaah! Unlimited Powaaaah! - Entropy 5<br /> <br /> So, you don't have a proper subject to download abilities from?<br /> <br /> Or perhaps you're trying to push the human limits, reaching were no one has ever braved before, going for that juicy 6+ lvls of a skill?<br /> <br /> Worry not! Just conjure up the knowledge out of no where with Entropy 5?<br /> <br /> How does that work? Who knows! Who cares? All that matters is that it works!<br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b<br /> (Yes, Entropy 5 can do that. How? Fate, luck, whatever. Doesn't matter. Maybe it conjures it up from the &quot;Cosmic Mind&quot; or the &quot;Collective Unconscious&quot;. The minutia is unimportant thou).<br /> <br /> Now, combine 3 and 2, and now you can conjure up any sort of knowledge you'd like out of the blue and store it all into crystal/your computer to use whenever you see fit!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-22T15:48:05-07:00","id":1544511,"title":"","content":"In my games, the Technocrats and the VA make extensive use of all the above. The Technocrats have extensive libraries of abilities for the use of their agents, held under 7 keys and dispensed upon need, while the VAs have a vast network of trade of abilities at the Web, which they trade among each other and even with other Traditions.<br /> <br /> That has created some awesome addition for my games, upon which the VAs became fencers oof skills. &quot;Damn, where shall we find someone proficient with rocket ballistics?&quot;. &quot;Don't worry, I know a guy...&quot;<br /> <br /> <br /> Finally, the least sophisticated method is to call a Spirit for it. That's not as simple as it sounds. Good luck finding a Spirit of &quot;rocketry ballistics&quot;...<br /> <br /> Once you found the proper spirit thou, and once you managed to strike a deal or subjugated it to do your bid (and deal with the consequences of either choice), then you can use Mind 3 and Prime to storage the knowledge for later use just the same.<br /> <br /> And finally, at last, if you're looking for something Matrix style, all that you need is the proper ability stored and Correspondence 3 to download it from afar.<br /> <br /> Have fun!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 10-22-2024, 06:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T07:53:04-07:00","id":1544556,"title":"","content":"I would say that, in the case of kung-fu or any other martial art, Mind is not enough. You need the physical conditioning, muscle memory, reflexes, etc. So I'd say Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T08:23:46-07:00","id":1544558,"title":"","content":"Depends on the Ability. As a rule of thumb, I could see Knowledges operating entirely off of Mind, while Skills and Talents require some Life as well. That said, I prefer to avoid mandatory conjunctional effects as much as possible, and would personally allow Mind to do it on its own \u2014 though maybe not as <i>easily</i> as a conjunctional effect: I have no problem with saying that something that might be a Standard Feat (requiring two successes) if you have both Mind and Life might be doable as a Difficult Feat (three successes) if you only have Mind.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T09:11:56-07:00","id":1544564,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544558#post1544558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the Ability. As a rule of thumb, I could see Knowledges operating entirely off of Mind, while Skills and Talents require some Life as well. That said, I prefer to avoid mandatory conjunctional effects as much as possible, and would personally allow Mind to do it on its own \u2014 though maybe not as <i>easily</i> as a conjunctional effect: I have no problem with saying that something that might be a Standard Feat (requiring two successes) if you have both Mind and Life might be doable as a Difficult Feat (three successes) if you only have Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a nice rule. It would be a lot easier to just reduce diff or increase attributes, which can be done with Life alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3153,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","user":"Lord Revan","date":". 10-23-2024, 12:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-23T15:13:46-07:00","id":1544596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544558#post1544558\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on the Ability. As a rule of thumb, I could see Knowledges operating entirely off of Mind, while Skills and Talents require some Life as well. That said, I prefer to avoid mandatory conjunctional effects as much as possible, and would personally allow Mind to do it on its own \u2014 though maybe not as <i>easily</i> as a conjunctional effect: I have no problem with saying that something that might be a Standard Feat (requiring two successes) if you have both Mind and Life might be doable as a Difficult Feat (three successes) if you only have Mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure this is why the game avoided increasing Abilities with magic. Trying to draw a line of when Mind is enough, and when it isn't is a lot to do.<br /> <br /> Medicine is a great example of a Knowledge that most certainly requires physical training to justify high dots. Hell, EpiPens, something designed specifically for people without medical training to use in emergencies, are really easy to do wrong if you've never actually practiced with a real one to have some memories of the physical sensation of what it feels like when you do it right. Performing surgery is something people train for years to do because it's not just theory and anatomy.<br /> <br /> Trying to parse out when Life and Mind are both valuable, or when one is enough, is adding a lot of overhead into figuring out how to handle trying to boost and action with magic. Boosting Attributes or reducing a specific roll's difficulty makes everything easier because then you're using whichever Sphere is most relevant to what you're actually doing than the broad range of what an Ability can do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T04:04:48-07:00","id":1544638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lord Revan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544556#post1544556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would say that, in the case of kung-fu or any other martial art, Mind is not enough. You need the physical conditioning, muscle memory, reflexes, etc. So I'd say Life.</div> </div> </div> </div>The skill is purely mental thou. You could download the skill with Mind. &quot;Muscle memory&quot; doesn't exist. Muscles don't have memories, only neurons do.<br /> <br /> Now, it is one thing to have the neurons for quick responses, and another to have the body fit for it, that much is true. You may have the brain reflexes of a Tiger, but if you have the body of a slug, then all you'll be able to do will be to know that it's going to hurt pretty bad very, very quickly.<br /> <br /> So, I would say that you can download and save a skill like Kung Fu with Mind and Prime alone, but to fully use it, you also need Life.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T04:16:54-07:00","id":1544639,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544596#post1544596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm pretty sure this is why the game avoided increasing Abilities with magic. Trying to draw a line of when Mind is enough, and when it isn't is a lot to do.<br /> <br /> Medicine is a great example of a Knowledge that most certainly requires physical training to justify high dots. Hell, EpiPens, something designed specifically for people without medical training to use in emergencies, are really easy to do wrong if you've never actually practiced with a real one to have some memories of the physical sensation of what it feels like when you do it right. Performing surgery is something people train for years to do because it's not just theory and anatomy.<br /> <br /> Trying to parse out when Life and Mind are both valuable, or when one is enough, is adding a lot of overhead into figuring out how to handle trying to boost and action with magic. Boosting Attributes or reducing a specific roll's difficulty makes everything easier because then you're using whichever Sphere is most relevant to what you're actually doing than the broad range of what an Ability can do.</div> </div> </div> </div>But here's the thing thou, all this &quot;training&quot; is inside your brain. It is NOT your fingers operating on their own. The difference between practice and theory is because when you're studying theory you're only grasping knowledge, when you're practicing your BRAIN is developing the connections that regulate the movement of your fingers. The brain is using the input from your eyes and the feeling on your hands to forge new synapses - but it is, again, inside your brain.<br /> <br /> A cat has a reaction time 10 times greater than a human. That's because their brain is up to the task.<br /> <br /> The role of the body is about muscular capacity to have EXPLOSIVE movement. It's the ability to move fast, to have a potent heart, strong muscles and strong skeleton and powerful lungs for the task, that would allow the body to react properly to the commands of the brain. Everything about reflexes thou, it is all inside the brain, not the body. The only thing the body does or does not is to be able to react properly.<br /> <br /> Think about &quot;bullet time&quot;. If you had the time reaction of the Flash, you could see the bullets flying in slow motion. But unless you yourself are as fast as The Flash, all you would be able to do would be to know that you're going to be pretty dead once they reach their destination, so you probably will use that looooong agonizing time to analyze your life and make your last prayers. (You might still be able to dodge BEFORE the bad guy shoots, once you see him reaching for his gun in slow motion thou)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T04:30:16-07:00","id":1544643,"title":"","content":"&quot;Muscle memory&quot; is a thing, even if the name is poor from a scientific perspective.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this treads deeply into the fact that Mage heavily embraces Mind/Body duality via the Spheres, but there's very little evidence for it in real life. Motor skill retention might be part of the nervous system... but the nervous system is still cells and bodily functions (Life)... so when does it become a Mind Pattern instead? And if anything the whole point of motor skill retention training in the first place is to encode tasks so that you don't have to actually think about them. Martial artists train up from the basics so they can encode each part of a &quot;punch&quot; into automated pathways so they can fire off a whole series of functions with minimal processing. Can you Mind download neural processes you don't even consciously think about doing? Or are those Life processes? Is downloading all of the individual steps of a punch with Mind the same as encoding them as a retained motor skill, or is that second part Life?<br /> <br /> Another way to look at the problem is that the WoD system in general treats Abilities as body intellectual knowledge of a subject, and experience with practical application of the subject. It's not hard to accommodate the Mind/Body dualism of Mage if there was some sort of neat separate between &quot;theory&quot; and &quot;practice&quot; on terms of how Abilities are expressed. But since the WoD system blends the two, the line between what's Life and what's Mind is ultimately going to be highly subjective.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> You're over-stressing the brain, as the whole nervous system is involved and not everything goes to the brain, as well as &quot;explosive&quot; movement (physical training also involves flexibility, bone strengthening, slow-twitch muscle exercises for endurance, etc.), and broad generalizations (all species have a spectrum of physical abilities, there isn't one reaction time for cats, and one for humans, and training can increase reaction times; at least in specific circumstances).<br /> <br /> You're not at all addressing Mind vs. Life as Spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 10-24-2024, 07:36 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T05:15:53-07:00","id":1544644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544643#post1544643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Muscle memory&quot; is a thing, even if the name is poor from a scientific perspective.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Its still stored in the brain, neuron paths, nothing more.<br /> As for doing things you are not thinking about, its still part of your mind.<br /> <br /> Then again Athlethics for example would be almost pure life. Its just a trained body with maybe some technique to it.<br /> <br /> Mind and life tend to blend thats why i often allow someone with life 4 to control the neurons in the brain affecting someones mood and personality. Maybe the correct answer is Data? Or Mind + Life always (in a spectrum that we can ignore).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T06:28:44-07:00","id":1544646,"title":"","content":"Well if you treat HDYDT as authorative (and for the record, I don't recommend it) awakened magic can't replicate muscle memory. In a baffling decision, even a Life 5/Mind 5 cloning process can only impart skills and memories, not the muscle memory to use them. I mean, regardless of whether muscle memory is Life, Mind, or some combination of the two, Life 5/Mind 5 should be able to handle it.<br /> <br /> If we are generous, it's possible that this is supposed to be a roundabout way of explaining an experience requirement (nevermind that experience isn't mentioned). If so, I would recommend ignoring anything the book says about muscle memory, let it be imparted with some combination of Life and Mind, and adapt the system for experience costs for Attribute boosting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T11:02:21-07:00","id":1544660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544644#post1544644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its still stored in the brain, neuron paths, nothing more.<br /> As for doing things you are not thinking about, its still part of your mind.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's largely avoiding what I was saying: in reality where mind-body dualism isn't really considered accurate, it's all well and dandy to say &quot;this is a process of the neural system.&quot; In Mage, where mind-body dualism is hard coded into the rules, the nervous system and the mind are not the same thing. Something that is purely done in the brain is not the same as something being a Mind Pattern that is primarily governed by Mind: you can't expel an infection of the brain with Mind, you need to use Life, even if the primary symptoms are neurological.<br /> <br /> You can't say, &quot;it's in your brain, thus it's in your mind, thus you use Mind,&quot; because that's not actually how the game is structured. That's not to say people arguing for Mind being the primary Sphere for the effect are wrong in that conclusion (Dream and Hypercram certainly imply there's more validity to that on their own) but that the explanations given for what Spheres to use don't really align with the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again Athlethics for example would be almost pure life. Its just a trained body with maybe some technique to it. </div> </div> </div>Like this. The whole point of Athletics is that it's the techniques that allow dedicated athletes to excel beyond their raw physicality (as expressed via Attributes). Dismissing the technique side of Athletics (and potentially any creative uses like knowledge of the rules of different sports, or similar trivia) to try to claim it's clearly a &quot;Life&quot; Ability doesn't match up with the text. &quot;Trained body&quot; isn't just physical fitness, it's techniques for various athletic endeavors. Anyone with high Dexterity can probably be a decent hitter in baseball, but you buy up Athletics to become a great hitter because you have technique both for making contact, and for knowing how different swings can be used for different strategies (knowing how to maximize your chances for a solid line drive vs. going for the fences vs. purposefully fouling the ball vs. bunting vs a purposeful midfield blooper are all things that come from technique, not just having a trained body).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe the correct answer is... </div> </div> </div>Really, there isn't a correct answer. As noted there's an answer that most closely aligns with the text (you can't actually do this directly), but as few of us seem satisfied with that answer, it quickly turns into the best answer being a personal one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T12:44:39-07:00","id":1544669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544643#post1544643\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Muscle memory&quot; is a thing, even if the name is poor from a scientific perspective.<br /> <br /> The problem is that this treads deeply into the fact that Mage heavily embraces Mind/Body duality via the Spheres, but there's very little evidence for it in real life. Motor skill retention might be part of the nervous system... but the nervous system is still cells and bodily functions (Life)... so when does it become a Mind Pattern instead?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, neurons are cells of the body, and synapses are metabolic processes.<br /> <br /> Mage seems to apply the Mind Sphere to anything with a synapse in it thou.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And if anything the whole point of motor skill retention training in the first place is to encode tasks so that you don't have to actually think about them. </div> </div> </div>There's no movements in your body that you do without &quot;thinking&quot;.<br /> <br /> What you're thinking about here is focusing your thoughts. We don't &quot;think&quot; when we walk. However, the body doesn't just simply move on its own.<br /> <br /> The thing is, you don't have to FOCUS your attention to do something like walking &quot;ok, first right leg, up and... Down. Very good. Now again with the left&quot;.<br /> <br /> But that doesn't mean that your legs aren't movie due to your conscious thoughts. They are. You just simply don't have to focus your entire attention to do it like the first time you're attempting brain surgery.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Martial artists train up from the basics so they can encode each part of a &quot;punch&quot; into automated pathways so they can fire off a whole series of functions with minimal processing. </div> </div> </div>That's the thing again thou, minimal processing does NOT mean no processing and that their fists become possessed by the spirit of Bruce Lee. It's the same as using your legs to walk, once more.<br /> <br /> By the way, we can only walk &quot;without thinking&quot; because we learned well enough how to do it without paying the least amount of attention. But for babies, that's an unsurmountable challenge, and they need to focus their entire brain capabilities in order to try it out.<br /> <br /> \u200b\u200b\u200b\u200bThe same holds true for people that suffered injuries in the spine that render them unable to walk for a long period. In case their body actually heals, they have to re-learn how to walk once again, because their brain will forget how to do it.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I say it again, it's brain, not the muscle.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you Mind download neural processes you don't even consciously think about doing? </div> </div> </div>Yes, absolutely. The entire process is stored under synaptic impulses in the brain. The muscles don't hold any sort of information <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Or are those Life processes? Is downloading all of the individual steps of a punch with Mind the same as encoding them as a retained motor skill, or is that second part Life? </div> </div> </div>Again, muscles have no memory. Any sort of body movement is controlled by the brain. Any and ALL of it. There are motor neurons that are specialized in just that. When you train your &quot;body&quot;, you are actually increasing the amount of pathways and connections between these neurons.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Edit:<br /> <br /> You're over-stressing the brain, as the whole nervous system is involved and not everything goes to the brain, as well as &quot;explosive&quot; movement (physical training also involves flexibility, bone strengthening, slow-twitch muscle exercises for endurance, etc.), and broad generalizations (all species have a spectrum of physical abilities, there isn't one reaction time for cats, and one for humans, and training can increase reaction times; at least in specific circumstances).<br /> <br /> You're not at all addressing Mind vs. Life as Spheres. </div> </div> </div>I really dislike that sort of nitpick. When I say &quot;brain&quot;, read &quot;nervous system&quot;. We are not in a scientific symposium, I'm saying &quot;brain&quot; very colloquially, but you understood perfect well what I meant.<br /> <br /> So, you understood what I meant by &quot;explosive movement&quot;. So why the need for the nitpick?<br /> <br /> Cats ON AVERAGE have a reaction time 10x faster than humans ON AVERAGE. It is obvious that individuals are variable, so this is so obvious that it DOESN'T NEED TO BE SAID. That's why that sort of nitpick is so annoying. It's like saying &quot;men have more muscle mass than women&quot; &quot;well, ackuthually...&quot; - IT'S ON AVERAGE FOR CHRIST'S SAKE!<br /> <br /> Back to cats thou, even the slowest one, unless he's physically impaired, is still faster than the fastest human, therefore the point still stands no matter what, so it really annoys me having to digress about such insignificant minutia while the focal point of the argument was perfectly understood - to the point that even you yourself was able to expand upon it, so there's really no point in going on those","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T12:52:04-07:00","id":1544670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544644#post1544644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its still stored in the brain, neuron paths, nothing more.<br /> As for doing things you are not thinking about, its still part of your mind.<br /> <br /> Then again Athlethics for example would be almost pure life. Its just a trained body with maybe some technique to it.<br /> <br /> Mind and life tend to blend thats why i often allow someone with life 4 to control the neurons in the brain affecting someones mood and personality. Maybe the correct answer is Data? Or Mind + Life always (in a spectrum that we can ignore).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, there's things that you would need a body fit for the commands of the... Ahem... Nervous system (got be a little pedantic here otherwise there will be an ACHKUALLY...being uttered out).<br /> <br /> You might have the neural pathways properly arranged for rapid movement, but your muscles and bones might disappoint.<br /> <br /> And here is my take: you already have the Attribute DEXTERITY. That's the part that relates to your body. The skill is purely &quot;mental&quot; (AKA the skill reflects the pathways of your neurons).<br /> <br /> So, you would need Life to increase your Dexterity; any abilities is Mind","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T12:54:50-07:00","id":1544671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544646#post1544646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well if you treat HDYDT as authorative (and for the record, I don't recommend it) awakened magic can't replicate muscle memory. In a baffling decision, even a Life 5/Mind 5 cloning process can only impart skills and memories, not the muscle memory to use them. I mean, regardless of whether muscle memory is Life, Mind, or some combination of the two, Life 5/Mind 5 should be able to handle it.<br /> <br /> If we are generous, it's possible that this is supposed to be a roundabout way of explaining an experience requirement (nevermind that experience isn't mentioned). If so, I would recommend ignoring anything the book says about muscle memory, let it be imparted with some combination of Life and Mind, and adapt the system for experience costs for Attribute boosting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damn. I didn't remember that. Probably because that book was sooooooo good that I decided to completely forget it exists.<br /> <br /> But even for someone like me without any sort of expectations for this book, I'm still disappointed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T13:07:23-07:00","id":1544672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544660#post1544660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But that's largely avoiding what I was saying: in reality where mind-body dualism isn't really considered accurate, it's all well and dandy to say &quot;this is a process of the neural system.&quot; In Mage, where mind-body dualism is hard coded into the rules, the nervous system and the mind are not the same thing. Something that is purely done in the brain is not the same as something being a Mind Pattern that is primarily governed by Mind: you can't expel an infection of the brain with Mind, you need to use Life, even if the primary symptoms are neurological.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I get what you mean, however ANY sort of movement of our body comes from our conscious thoughts. The exception are the... Well, I don't know the names in English, but are the automatic process, yes they are regulated by the nervous system but they are NOT conscious, like your heart beating and the contractions of your intestines.<br /> <br /> You're mistaking &quot;low attention&quot; to &quot;automatic&quot;. You'll never see someone running uncontrollably on the streets screaming &quot;somebody please help! My legs won't stop!&quot;. The fact that we say COLLOQUIALLY that we &quot;don't need to think to walk&quot; doesn't mean you aren't really thinking when you do it.<br /> <br /> Also, I've done martial arts and I know what it means to act &quot;by reflex&quot;. And sometimes I do react &quot;without thinking&quot;, because I have really honed my reflexes, so my &quot;body&quot; reacts before I have time to &quot;think&quot;. (Seriously, I once even dropped a friend on the floor that tried jokingly to grab my neck from behind. I only understood what happened when he was on the floor).<br /> <br /> But that's not really what's happening. My reflexes are simply faster than my conscious thoughts, but that's still my mind acting. So much so that I wouldn't be able to do the things I do while blindfolded and with earplugs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T14:28:26-07:00","id":1544684,"title":"","content":"And yet, you still refuse to address mind-body dualism... so what's the point of all that typing?<br /> <br /> If Mind covers everything governed by the nervous system...and Life governs everything else in the body... that's not in the text anywhere. Mind pretty much becomes OP when it comes to dealing with anything that classifies as having a Mind, since even automated responses like heart rate can be manipulated by influencing conscious functions (why bother using Life or Forces to attack people when you can use Mind to coincidentally kill people via sudden extreme stress response?).<br /> <br /> Getting snide about me not reading your mind when you insist on using one term and really meant a different term doesn't really feel that justified when you're just going to skip the core of what I'm saying to bemoan nitpicking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T17:53:44-07:00","id":1544694,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544684#post1544684\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And yet, you still refuse to address mind-body dualism... so what's the point of all that typing?<br /> <br /> If Mind covers everything governed by the nervous system...and Life governs everything else in the body... that's not in the text anywhere. Mind pretty much becomes OP when it comes to dealing with anything that classifies as having a Mind, since even automated responses like heart rate can be manipulated by influencing conscious functions (why bother using Life or Forces to attack people when you can use Mind to coincidentally kill people via sudden extreme stress response?).<br /> <br /> Getting snide about me not reading your mind when you insist on using one term and really meant a different term doesn't really feel that justified when you're just going to skip the core of what I'm saying to bemoan nitpicking.</div> </div> </div> </div>One could argue that you can kill using Mind. You CAN, after all, cause REAL damage with purely mental illusions.<br /> <br /> Yes, you could use Mind to cause a stress response that kills someone. The rules already address that, each success causes 2 bashing damage. That can be in the form of an illusion of a bullet or under a severe induced panic attack, it matters not.<br /> <br /> That indeed can be used to easily kill SLEEPERS. But then again, so can Life 3 cause a direct heart attack and it would be much easier because it would cause Lethal damage, but I don't see anybody saying that this is OP.<br /> <br /> The reason being that it ain't so easy to kill other critters of the night with such cheap magics. Sleepers are easy picks, other Mages or something more on the weird side of things like Bloodsuckers and the big hounds however would laugh it off.<br /> <br /> I was not getting snide. I apologize for my tone. It just bother me, but ok. If you want to get specific, then we could say that, under scientific terms (just for our of game easier understanding, not to discount in game mystics), then Mind would control everything in the nervous system that isn't part of the autonomous systems (like the control of breathing, control of heart, glands or the movements of the intestines).<br /> <br /> And no, I'm not saying that the text says this. It doesn't. But that's the consequences of what it applies to are. It involves everything related to the consciousness, and that's what it entails.<br /> <br /> Can you, therefore, alter someone's mind to indirectly alter the body? Yes, absolutely. Like causing a stress induced heart attack. Just like you can use Life 3 to induce euphoria into someone by discharging adrenaline into their bodies. But that's an indirect control however. You're not really turning the mind of the person into a state of euphoria, you're just injecting adrenaline, the euphoria is just an indirect consequence. That would be saying like that you use Forces to turn wood into ashes. Yes, that's what fire does to wood, that's the consequence of burning it.<br /> <br /> About being able to induce a heart attack coincidentally, that might as well be the case of your target has a history of panic attacks of severe anxiety, however I don't think it would be that coincidental to try to do it against someone that has never had a history of mental diseases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-24T18:29:13-07:00","id":1544698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544694#post1544694\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to get specific, then we could say that, under scientific terms (just for our of game easier understanding, not to discount in game mystics), then Mind would control everything in the nervous system that isn't part of the autonomous systems (like the control of breathing, control of heart, glands or the movements of the intestines).</div> </div> </div> </div>Why should we say this though? It causes a lot of interpretive problems with the line between Life and Mind, and requires even more knowledge by the players of the game to know how to adjudicate effects.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But that's the consequences of what it applies to are. It involves everything related to the consciousness, and that's what it entails. </div> </div> </div>Except, again, mind-body dualism ends this line of consequences. The mind isn't the same as the nervous system in Mage. There is a poorly defined arbitrary line between body and mind, between Life and Mind, that ends the line of implications from what's in the text to straight up say that non-autonomous nervous system = Mind. The structure of the Mind Sphere doesn't really do that much implying in this direction in the first place though: Reading subconscious thoughts is significantly harder than reading conscious thoughts, even as you've pointed out subconscious thoughts primarily exist to reduce the load on the neural system and are thus simpler biologically. Magic usually goes in the opposite direction where the simpler the system the easier it is to deal with; thus implying a serious disconnect between the mind and the body instead (and of course the fact that Mind lets you pick up emotions from objects that were exposed to emotional interactions furthers this).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Can you, therefore, alter someone's mind to indirectly alter the body? </div> </div> </div>But you're arguing for the ability to directly alter the body by letting the nervous system fall under the purview of Mind. If Mind alone can instantly encode motor skill retention, it's directly altering the body of the target. Downloading Abilities isn't indirectly altering the target like making them sad will also increase hormonal responses the body naturally produces in response to experiencing sadness. Downloading Abilities is directly manipulating bio-chemical pathways.<br /> <br /> If I want to make someone immune to a disease with magic, Life is all I need (how much depending on the disease) because Life clearly gives control over living bodies and that obviously includes adjustments to the immune system. The only difference between this and downloading Abilities is the base claim that because it's the nervous system it should be different. You're not making a case for that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-25T05:16:38-07:00","id":1544719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544698#post1544698\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why should we say this though? It causes a lot of interpretive problems with the line between Life and Mind, and requires even more knowledge by the players of the game to know how to adjudicate effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you think so? I think it's a lot simpler and much more cut and dry, but perhaps that's because I'm only looking at it with my own mind and my own way of viewing things and not being able to understand how others would see. What are exactly the objections you would have? For me, &quot;all non-autonomous&quot; seems pretty clear, but if you may please elaborate that would help me see the problems in it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Except, again, mind-body dualism ends this line of consequences. The mind isn't the same as the nervous system in Mage. There is a poorly defined arbitrary line between body and mind, between Life and Mind, that ends the line of implications from what's in the text to straight up say that non-autonomous nervous system = Mind. </div> </div> </div>Ah, ok. Yes, in here I was not 100% clear. No, Im NOT saying that &quot;Mind governs all non-autonomous&quot;. And that's PRECISELY because of Mind/Body dualism.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying however is that those COINCIDE - AKA the areas that the... &quot;Antropic Field&quot; or &quot;Soul&quot; or &quot;Mind&quot; are, are the same of those that, in the body, provoke responses in these systems.<br /> <br /> I don't know if I made myself clear now, did you understand that part? Maybe I can try to clarify a bit more, this is indeed a complex issue, and if anyone believes in Mind/Body dualism - which I myself particularly don't - it would be clearly something hard to explain. For a mechanicist materialist like me, it's much easier, &quot;consciousness&quot; is just an emergent pattern that arises from the sum of all the parts of the nervous system - aka it's just the collective of synapses between neurons. Therefore, trying to explain a hypothetical Mind/Body dualism is indeed complex, but I hope I managed to make it clear my position.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The structure of the Mind Sphere doesn't really do that much implying in this direction in the first place though: Reading subconscious thoughts is significantly harder than reading conscious thoughts, even as you've pointed out subconscious thoughts primarily exist to reduce the load on the neural system and are thus simpler biologically. </div> </div> </div>But then again, MtA indeed uses Mind/Body dualism as you have rightfully pointed out, thus biological responses aren't directly tied to mental patterns, even thou they are connected. Therefore, even thou subconscious thoughts are less biologically prevalent, in the &quot;quantum field&quot; of the technobabble Mind, it might be the reverse. It is pseudoscience/mysticism at the end of the day.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Magic usually goes in the opposite direction where the simpler the system the easier it is to deal with; thus implying a serious disconnect between the mind and the body instead (and of course the fact that Mind lets you pick up emotions from objects that were exposed to emotional interactions furthers this). </div> </div> </div>Yeah, the Mind Sphere isn't biological. Not just that you can pick up emotions from objects, you can imprint emotions in objects or even places, you can create &quot;auras&quot; of emotions but much more than just that, you can actually separate mind and body and float as pure though in the ether, which is just pure fantasy/mysticism. You can even create minds without a body.<br /> <br /> Body/Mind dualism is therefore firmly established by the game; that's not my point thou, my point is simply that the Mind coincides with the biological parts that control the non autonomous systems of the nervous system, NOT that it IS that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But you're arguing for the ability to directly alter the body by letting the nervous system fall under the purview of Mind. If Mind alone can instantly encode motor skill retention, it's directly altering the body of the target. Downloading Abilities isn't indirectly altering the target like making them sad will also increase hormonal responses the body naturally produces in response to experiencing sadness. Downloading Abilities is directly manipulating bio-chemical pathways. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, now I see that I miscommunicated. But I guess now it is more clear what I meant. No, Mind Sphere do NOT &quot;control&quot; the non-autonomous parts of the nervous system, but the &quot;Consciousness&quot; (the &quot;Mind&quot; in the game) coincides with those parts.<br /> <br /> I guess that the problem is that this &quot;dualism&quot; isn't real, it's just mysticism, and in rl scientific terms, &quot;consciousness&quot; is the emergent pattern of these parts. Hence why it is problematic to try to explain such mystical hypothesis.<br /> <br /> Controlling motor responses however is NOT &quot;controlling the body&quot;. Otherwise you would need Life to control someone, which isn't the case.<br /> <br /> Now, with Mind 4 you can control somebody's Mind right? Well, it just so happens that the enthralled victim will obey your commands... Including MOVING IN THE WAY YOU TELL THEM TO.<br /> <br /> It's the Mind that &quot;commands&quot; the body. The body doesn't move by its own - even thou they are technically &quot;disconnected&quot; in the game.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I want to make someone immune to a disease with magic, Life is all I need (how much depending on the disease) because Life clearly gives control over living bodies and that obviously includes adjustments to the immune system. The only difference between this and downloading Abilities is the base claim that because it's the nervous system it should be different. You're not making a case for that. </div> </div> </div>You're focusing too much on the idea of &quot;nervous system&quot; and, based on my perception (which may be wrong) the idea of &quot;muscle memory&quot;, but like I said, such a thing doesn't exist. It seems we are arguing semantics here and because of that there's being a serious miscommunication between both of us, where we are each one of us saying one thing and the other is understanding another, but I think I'm beginning to get where you are at.<br /> <br /> The problem is that you believe in this notion of &quot;muscle memory&quot;, or that certain motor facilities are controlled by a sort of more &quot;autonomous systems&quot;. But such is not the case however. The runner doesn't run because his legs are moving by their own. He moves with intent, by conscious choice. It's his mind that orders the body around. It doesn't matter that he has practiced for years and thus can &quot;run better&quot; than a normal person because he has internalized techniques and whatnot, to a point he doesn't even need to think about those and just naturally, instinctively use them.<br /> <br /> In scientific terms however, that aptitude is just simply an increased number of pathways between the neurons of the motor functions. It's not the body, the muscles and skeleton that get a &quot;memory&quot; of the motions, but rather the Mind that gets sharper in doing these.<br /> <br /> There are things that you do need some help from the body: for a marksman for instance, having a steady hand is essential.<br /> <br /> However, the ability to spot a target and aim with precision is purely mental.<br /> <br /> That dichotomy in game terms is easily represented by:<br /> Body: Dexterity (steady hand, flexibility, explosive muscular fast response and so on)<br /> Mind: Abilities <br /> <br /> That's precisely why Dexterity is a Physical Attribute rather than a mental one, because Dexterity is NOT &quot;Reflexes&quot; per se, which would be a mental attribute, and is probably more defined by Wits","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 10-25-2024, 02:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T05:23:21-07:00","id":1544789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544719#post1544719\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you think so? I think it's a lot simpler and much more cut and dry, but perhaps that's because I'm only looking at it with my own mind and my own way of viewing things and not being able to understand how others would see. What are exactly the objections you would have? For me, &quot;all non-autonomous&quot; seems pretty clear, but if you may please elaborate that would help me see the problems in it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As you address later, the game runs on Mind-Body dualism which makes this significantly more complicated. As well, most people don't have any real training in neurology to know where the lines really are. What's &quot;subconscious but still thinking,&quot; vs. &quot;subconscious but autonomous&quot; isn't something most people know about everything our body does. It doesn't help that there are some very obvious bodily functions that can be both: breathing, for example, can by controlled by our autonomous neural pathways and conscious pathways. Then there's indirect control where we can't consciously control our heart rate directly, but we can consciously influence it fast or slower by engaging pathways that have indirect impact on our hearts. Most people do not have the anatomical and neurological knowledge to get the difference between &quot;you can train yourself to only think 'walk' and not have to consciously think of each step in the process of walking,&quot; and those steps not becoming &quot;autonomous&quot; after the &quot;walk&quot; command is issued because it relies on technical vs. common terminology.<br /> <br /> Then you layer how Mage's Spheres are actually written on top of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Ah, ok. Yes, in here I was not 100% clear. No, Im NOT saying that &quot;Mind governs all non-autonomous&quot;. And that's PRECISELY because of Mind/Body dualism.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying however is that those COINCIDE - AKA the areas that the... &quot;Antropic Field&quot; or &quot;Soul&quot; or &quot;Mind&quot; are, are the same of those that, in the body, provoke responses in these systems. </div> </div> </div>That stands in stark contrast to the idea that you can magically give yourself Skills with just Mind though; which you were arguing for. If Mind operates on the body indirectly, then all motor skills associated with an Abilities can only be acquired faster/maintained easier with Mind, but the actual encoding would still be Life because that's a direct process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't know if I made myself clear now, did you understand that part? Maybe I can try to clarify a bit more, this is indeed a complex issue, and if anyone believes in Mind/Body dualism - which I myself particularly don't - it would be clearly something hard to explain. For a mechanicist materialist like me, it's much easier, &quot;consciousness&quot; is just an emergent pattern that arises from the sum of all the parts of the nervous system - aka it's just the collective of synapses between neurons. Therefore, trying to explain a hypothetical Mind/Body dualism is indeed complex, but I hope I managed to make it clear my position. </div> </div> </div>So, the biggest thing I'm confused about is that it feels like you're trying to have to conversations at the same time: one about how mind-body dualism is wrong, and one about how to handle Mage.<br /> <br /> Because it doesn't matter what you belief about our reality (or what I believe, and I'm not a mind-body dualist either). I'm talking about the game, and all the debating of real world stuff is sometimes a meaningful tangent, but should never override the focus on the point of how to play the game itself. The game is mind-body dualistic, and we have to approach discussions of how to handle the rules from that standpoint even if that's not how we think the real world works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Body/Mind dualism is therefore firmly established by the game; that's not my point thou, my point is simply that the Mind coincides with the biological parts that control the non autonomous systems of the nervous system, NOT that it IS that. </div> </div> </div>Again though, that means the direct coding of motor skills would primarily be Life, with Mind backing it up. Mind would only be able to indirectly influence the process.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hence why it is problematic to try to explain such mystical hypothesis. </div> </div> </div>That is, however, the point of the thread.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Controlling motor responses however is NOT &quot;controlling the body&quot;. Otherwise you would need Life to control someone, which isn't the case. </div> </div> </div>Well, sometimes you do need Life to control someone, even if the base effect is Mind. But Mind doesn't let you control someone like a puppet. You can issue orders, and their minds will follow said orders by operating their bodies accordingly. You can't use Mind to make someone do something they're not capable of just by ordering them to. It's still an indirect form of controlling their body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You're focusing too much on the idea of &quot;nervous system&quot; and, based on my perception (which may be wrong) the idea of &quot;muscle memory&quot;, but like I said, such a thing doesn't exist. </div> </div> </div>How can I be the only overly focused on the &quot;idea&quot; of the nervous system when you're the only that keeps coming back to it and refused to engage with how the rest of the body interacts with it; esp. when it comes to motor skills?<br /> <br /> I also haven't talked about muscle memory in more than a few posts. And still, muscle memory is real, it's just a bad pop culture name for motor skill retention.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> ...but I think I'm beginning to get where you are at. </div> </div> </div>I'm doubting this significantly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that you believe in this notion of &quot;muscle memory&quot;, or that certain motor facilities are controlled by a sort of more &quot;autonomous systems&quot;. But such is not the case however. The runner doesn't run because his legs are moving by their own. He moves with intent, by conscious choice. It's his mind that orders the body around. It doesn't matter that he has practiced for years and thus can &quot;run better&quot; than a normal person because he has internalized techniques and whatnot, to a point he doesn't even need to think about those and just naturally, instinctively use them. </div> </div> </div>Like this. &quot;Muscle memory&quot; is just a pop culture phrase for this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In scientific terms however, that aptitude is just simply an increased number of pathways between the neurons of the motor functions. It's not the body, the muscles and skeleton that get a &quot;memory&quot; of the motions, but rather the Mind that gets sharper in doing these. </div> </div> </div>Nobody talking about muscle memory believes that muscles have a literal memory storage system. They don't think legs just &quot;run&quot; on their own. They get that the nervous system is in control. But since they haven't studied and kept current on neurology, they don't know all those specifics and the phrase is a good-enough-shorthand for what's going on to grasp for their practical needs: if you train your body to do X, it will get better at doing X. Treating them like idiots because they don't care to take a university level course on neurological anatomy and function is a statement on yourself (and yes, that's my current understanding of your intentions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, the ability to spot a target and aim with precision is purely mental. </div> </div> </div>... no, it's a complex combination of both physical and mental aptitudes.<br /> <br /> You cannot acquire targets, and shoot with precision and accuracy with just your mind. Precision shooting especially comes from motor skill retention. The Internet went nuts over a Turkish Olympic shooter's stance this year because it was so different from the kinda ridiculous optimized stances younger shooters use now. But it's incredibly important to be able to hold that position exactly (hence him keeping with an older stance and things like using his pocket as a reference point for his off hand's location) because that body control reduces the mental variables to make the shot. If you haven't conditioned your body, and your arm is waving around because you can't hold it still in front of you, your brain is never going to calculate the shot fast enough to make up for your arm muscles twitching from the exertion of holding the gun still and you'll miss wildly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That dichotomy in game terms is easily represented by:<br /> Body: Dexterity (steady hand, flexibility, explosive muscular fast response and so on)<br /> Mind: Abilities </div> </div> </div>Or, rather, as the rules already do:<br /> <br /> Dexterity as the dominant Physical Attribute for shooting (explicitly able to be boosted by Life) and Perception as a secondary Mental Attribute for when you have time to aim a shot (specifically you can add 1 bonus die to your Dexterity + Firearms roll to shoot per turn spent aiming, up to a maximum of your Perception score); and Mental Attributes can already be boosted by Mind.<br /> <br /> The books already divvy up the Attributes along the three groupings. Abilities are in silos primarily defined by how well a normal person can perform without training and thus represent a different area of differentiation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's precisely why Dexterity is a Physical Attribute rather than a mental one, because Dexterity is NOT &quot;Reflexes&quot; per se, which would be a mental attribute, and is probably more defined by Wits </div> </div> </div>According to the books, reflexes are both Attribute categories depending on the reflex in question. This is pretty intuitive with the array of reflexes out there. Muscle stretch reflexes are pretty much only going to be rolled as part of a Dexterity check regarding keeping balance since those reflexes only come up in macro-actions that involve body position. The muscular tension reflex is pretty much what you're rolling Stamina for when you roll soak. The ocular reflexes are mostly going to come up in Perception rolls, and the startle reflex is fairly clearly governed by Wits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T11:20:30-07:00","id":1544803,"title":"","content":"This is quite a lot here so lets go one thing at a time:<br /> <br /> Nervous system and Mind/Life.<br /> <br /> I dont believe it is important to have precise knowledge in the subject. Life can affect nereves. Doing so it can affect mood and personality. Mind on the other hand for me is always solely the brain. Muscle memory is contained in the brain. The brain can affect the body but only in ways the target would be capable of when given orders and thats it.<br /> <br /> I think it would be even fair to treat Mind as a pattern sphere of its own as pattern locking someones mind can come in handy and would explain a lot of Mind in psionics of HDYDT.<br /> <br /> Dexterity and shooting<br /> I believe that we use Wits to shoot firearms in WOD not Dex.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T13:30:45-07:00","id":1544811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544803#post1544803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mind on the other hand for me is always solely the brain.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you mean specifically the brain, or like MM before do you mean it more broadly? Because this is where that detailed knowledge thing comes into play. As well, Mage does not consider the mind as an emergent property of the brain, but a separate phenomenon (hence the mind can leave traces of itself on objects outside the body the mind is connected to and so on). A lot of what happens in the brain really don't matter to what players are going to use the Mind Sphere for, and there's plenty of things the Mind Sphere does that extend past the strict confines of the brain when in it comes to how manipulating consciousness impacts the body that Mind Pattern is attached to.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Muscle memory is contained in the brain. </div> </div> </div>No, it's not. That's part of the problem with calling it &quot;memory&quot; in the first place. The majority of what we call muscle memory is performed by the motor neurons in the spinal column rather than sending things all the way up to the brain. The brain is of course involved as the center of executive function on deciding when to initiate and stop motor skills, but the retention of those skills is distributed across the CNS and relies heavily on constant feedback from the peripheral nerves (specifically the sensory neurons that are embedded in each muscle strand). <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think it would be even fair to treat Mind as a pattern sphere of its own as pattern locking someones mind can come in handy and would explain a lot of Mind in psionics of HDYDT. </div> </div> </div>The concept of &quot;Pattern Spheres&quot; has always been a bit of bad writing in the game, as the game also refers to anything the strictly falls under [Sphere] as a [Sphere Pattern]. Spirit is a &quot;Pattern Sphere&quot; when dealing with spirits and the Umbra because those are Spirit Patterns.<br /> <br /> The cluster of Life/Forces/Matter is really just about the Spheres that govern Patterns that are dictated by classic mechanics instead of other realms of physics and/or straight up metaphysics.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I believe that we use Wits to shoot firearms in WOD not Dex. </div> </div> </div>This is not correct. While Mage has the most advanced/optional rules for non-Dex based shooting as it's the game most likely to deal in operating weapons that exceed the standard personal weapons most games deal with (if a HIT Mark is equipped with guided munitions, it's not aiming those with Dex), the default Attribute for ranged attacks is Dex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T16:34:17-07:00","id":1544818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544811#post1544811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you mean specifically the brain, or like MM before do you mean it more broadly? Because this is where that detailed knowledge thing comes into play. As well, Mage does not consider the mind as an emergent property of the brain, but a separate phenomenon (hence the mind can leave traces of itself on objects outside the body the mind is connected to and so on). A lot of what happens in the brain really don't matter to what players are going to use the Mind Sphere for, and there's plenty of things the Mind Sphere does that extend past the strict confines of the brain when in it comes to how manipulating consciousness impacts the body that Mind Pattern is attached to.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, it's not. That's part of the problem with calling it &quot;memory&quot; in the first place. The majority of what we call muscle memory is performed by the motor neurons in the spinal column rather than sending things all the way up to the brain. The brain is of course involved as the center of executive function on deciding when to initiate and stop motor skills, but the retention of those skills is distributed across the CNS and relies heavily on constant feedback from the peripheral nerves (specifically the sensory neurons that are embedded in each muscle strand).<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Its stored in the cerebellum and thats part of the brain brain not the spine.<br /> <br /> I did mean just the brain. For me Mind is dual, its everything inside the brain but thanks to magic it also does not need the brain. The brain just makes it mundane, coincidental. Like a control panel for the mind. Therefore Mind can affect the body and the body can affect the mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28439,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","user":"quelsec","date":". 10-26-2024, 07:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T17:26:49-07:00","id":1544825,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544789#post1544789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...stuff...<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's... Too much. And there's yet another answer, I won't be able to find due time to deal with each point. There is however something I would like to address:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544789#post1544789\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, sometimes you do need Life to control someone, even if the base effect is Mind. But Mind doesn't let you control someone like a puppet. You can issue orders, and their minds will follow said orders by operating their bodies accordingly. You can't use Mind to make someone do something they're not capable of just by ordering them to. It's still an indirect form of controlling their body.</div> </div> </div> </div>Here I would have to say that you're wrong, and I believe that this point is enough to sum up my entire argument, because I believe it puts the doubts to rest.<br /> <br /> You CAN, in fact, control somebody like a Puppet using Mind 4. You can &quot;possess&quot; the Mind of the victim and thus control its body as if it were your own; if you're Mind... Astral-travelling? You can &quot;enter&quot; the victim as if you were a ghost possessing him. With Mind 1 effect &quot;Multiple Minds&quot;, you can even control several different bodies at once (including your own of course). Or you can use Mind 5 to sever your Mind from body and either enter an empty body (possibly created using Life 5) or use the same Mind 5 to rip off the Mind of a victim and then latch on to the now free real estate.<br /> <br /> I believe that proves that all motor actions from the body can only be commanded by the Mind; besides, if you enter the body of a Martial Artist using Mind 4 or 5, you won't learn Kung Fu from his body, because there's nothing there, the body holds no memories. And that is present in the books, when you do &quot;possess&quot; someone in this manner, you inherit ONLY the victim's physical attributes and appearance and nothing else; the other 2 social attributes, all the mental attributes and ALL OF YOUR ABILITIES will remain the same as before getting your new body. And that has always been the rule, which I believe puts the argument to rest.<br /> <br /> Edit: with a Mind 1 + Mind 4 effect, you can control a victim like a puppet, placing the victim's mind &quot;on the back seat&quot; without the need to Astral Travel and possessing the victim. Doing so, you can control both your own body AND your victim's body with your conscious thoughts as if it were your own. It's up to you if the victim's mind will be &quot;slumbering&quot; during the whole ordeal, or if you'll force her to become an unwilling and conscious observer of this horror thriller.<br /> <br /> So yes, all motor functions are controlled by the Mind, not the body.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":28035,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","user":"Magus Maximus","date":". 10-26-2024, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-26T18:15:26-07:00","id":1544826,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544818#post1544818\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its stored in the cerebellum and thats part of the brain brain not the spine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, based on what?<br /> <br /> Studies of damage to the cerebellum demonstrate reduced efficiency at performing motor skills, not forgetting retained motor skills: if you take damage to your cerebellum, you don't forget how to walk, but your walking grows uncoordinated and disorganized. Damage to the spinal column does result in the loss of retention of motor skills and if healing is possible, requires physical therapy to reestablish those motor skill pathways.<br /> <br /> Even motor skills that are retained in the brain are retained more in the brain stem, not the cerebellum, and the division between the brain stem and the spinal column is fairly arbitrary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me Mind is dual, its everything inside the brain but thanks to magic it also does not need the brain. The brain just makes it mundane, coincidental. Like a control panel for the mind. Therefore Mind can affect the body and the body can affect the mind. </div> </div> </div>Nobody is arguing against Mind and Life effects bridging the mind-body divide, but what you're saying isn't well supported in the book.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544825#post1544825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You CAN, in fact, control somebody like a Puppet using Mind 4.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you can't. M20 specifically calls for Life as well as mind to fully possess another living being. Mind can make someone sleepy, but you need Life to make someone fall asleep immediately. Etc.<br /> <br /> Your whole argument that Mind alone lets you control all motor functions simply isn't supported.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T06:13:35-07:00","id":1544840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544826#post1544826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> No, you can't. M20 specifically calls for Life as well as mind to fully possess another living being. Mind can make someone sleepy, but you need Life to make someone fall asleep immediately. Etc.<br /> <br /> Your whole argument that Mind alone lets you control all motor functions simply isn't supported.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage 20th anniversary</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022</b> <b>Control Conscious Mind/<br /> Alter Consciousness/ Astral Projection</b><br /> The fearsome power of Black Suits and psychic assailants allows the mage to <u>command another person\u2019s actions as well as her thoughts, alter her perceptions or mental state, and project his own mind from his physical form.</u> At this Rank, a mage can change someone\u2019s memories, drive her crazy (or sane), overlay her aura with a desired impression, and set up posthypnotic suggestions and commands. (See Social Conditioning and Reprograming, pp. 605-607.) And by using internal rather than external powers, <u>he can also project his astral form</u>, as detailed in Chapter Nine, pp. 476-478.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Control Subconscious/ Forge Psyche/ Un-tether Consciousness</b><br /> A true Mind Master commands not only his own conscious<br /> but other minds as well. He may alter someone\u2019s mind forever, raising (or lowering) her Traits, rewriting her personality, changing her Nature Trait, <u>or (with Life 4) switching her mind into another body.</u> He can do the same things to his own mind as well, and he can untether that mind to explore the deeper reaches of astral space for hours or even days at a time. His greatest power, though, is the ability to fabricate entire consciousnesses, creating minds where no mind had been before.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forgive me, but you are mistaken here. I don't blame you thou, M20 is absolutely awful at the most important part for the game - explaining the possible effects from Spheres. Everything else, all of its 600+ pages could go to the garbage can if only they had made a good session about the Spheres, but sadly out of all editions, it was the absolutely worse of all of them.<br /> <br /> That's how we ended up with the book &quot;How do you do that&quot;, which is even worse somehow.<br /> <br /> It's a pitty really, M20 is really good at everything else, and that's important no doubt, but the most important part - the Spheres - it did a lousy job, as if the writers inferred that the players already knew how things work (and that no new players would begin by M20)<br /> <br /> I'm however a veteran of the previous editions - the ones that did explain how things actually work.<br /> <br /> And yes, you can indeed &quot;possess&quot; someone with Mind 4 alone. That has ALWAYS been the case ever since the first edition, and continues to be so.<br /> <br /> What the poor text of M20 says, which is why I wouldn't use it as a source, is that you need Life 4 to CONNECT A MIND TO A BODY - but the text here is too vague to be properly understood, I admit. Perhaps this is the reason as to why you have your opinion, and that's to no fault of your own, but due to the poor text. Now I see where the crux of the problem lies.<br /> <br /> That's NOT &quot;possessing&quot; someone, that's permanently switching bodies. That's a totally different process.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mind 4 allows you to &quot;possess&quot; someone and control the victim as a puppet; that has always been the case ever since the first edition, and there's no real indication that it has changed in M20, neither do the text in M20 even say otherwise. In fact, the text doesn't say anything about &quot;possession&quot;.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, it has also always been the case that in order to connect Mind and Body you need Mind and Life - but that's different from Possession. That's permanently fusing a Mind inside of a Body. This, again, has always been the case ever since the first edition too, and as the underlined parts which I brought about M20, continues to be the case.<br /> <br /> The problem is that previous editions had a part describing each level, followed by a session describing the possible effects of each level. That last part has been absent from M20, possibly due to the need to compact the already long manuscript, but that was essential to the full understanding of each Sphere, since sometimes some things were only understood by the effects they could do.<br /> <br /> Now I understand where your arguing from, and I see that you're arguing in good faith, based on what the rules as written appear to be; but that's more due to lack of explanation from the M20 text than what it was really meant to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T14:44:42-07:00","id":1544870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Magus Maximus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544840#post1544840\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Forgive me, but you are mistaken here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seems pretty clear that I'm right, but you don't like that M20 phrased things differently from older editions. I'm not mistaken for using the wording of the most current edition of the game.<br /> <br /> [quote]...as if the writers inferred that the players already knew how things work (and that no new players would begin by M20)[/quote<br /> <br /> The 20th books were largely written from the default that they were for existing fans, not new ones. That's why they're Anniversary editions that focused on being omnibus collections more than being proper new editions that advanced the game forward in design (though C20 and Wr20 got more leeway since neither of those games got a Revised edition).<br /> <br /> M20 was also headed by the most prolific Mage: the Ascension developer by a huge margin. Brucato's style might be... annoying... but he's basically the only real authority on how Mage is &quot;supposed&quot; to be, considering he wrote half of 1e, headed all of 2e and Sorcerer's Crusade, and then came back to head M20 as well. If it's between some Internet rando and Brucato, Brucato's words win.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm however a veteran of the previous editions - the ones that did explain how things actually work. </div> </div> </div>I've been playing Mage for 28 years. Shove it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And yes, you can indeed &quot;possess&quot; someone with Mind 4 alone. That has ALWAYS been the case ever since the first edition, and continues to be so. </div> </div> </div>And every edition established levels of possession; with variation in what you can do with each, how the target can resist, and so on.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What the poor text of M20 says, which is why I wouldn't use it as a source, is that you need Life 4 to CONNECT A MIND TO A BODY - but the text here is too vague to be properly understood, I admit. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that includes connecting your mind into another person's body to the point where you can ride it around like your own body.<br /> <br /> Previous editions didn't come with that caveat, but made it clear that trying to control motor actions with Mind 4 was obviously uncoordinated compared to simply issuing commands and letting the target enact the orders. Phrases like, &quot;cause an arm to twitch,&quot; are not full possession of the target's body's motor systems.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's NOT &quot;possessing&quot; someone, that's permanently switching bodies. That's a totally different process. </div> </div> </div>No, that's a different amount of successes for the difference between doing something temporary vs. something permanent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The problem is that previous editions had a part describing each level, followed by a session describing the possible effects of each level. That last part has been absent from M20, possibly due to the need to compact the already long manuscript, but that was essential to the full understanding of each Sphere, since sometimes some things were only understood by the effects they could do. </div> </div> </div>I get why you don't like the change ,but the did put most of those effects in the common effects chart instead of clustering them with the Spheres. That's where the &quot;compel sleepiness&quot; vs. &quot;put the target to sleep immediately&quot; example I used came from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Now I understand where your arguing from, and I see that you're arguing in good faith, based on what the rules as written appear to be; but that's more due to lack of explanation from the M20 text than what it was really meant to be. </div> </div> </div>And now I understand that you're arguing in complete bad faith because you only care about promoting your opinions, truth, reality, and the text of the game be damned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T15:47:53-07:00","id":1544871,"title":"","content":"So\u2026 I find it interesting that people are arguing about specifics of human biology in the context of a game where anything too specific is arguably a factor of one's worldview rather than an objective truth. <br /> <br /> Forget about the specific details about the human nervous system. That's a Progenitors thing. To a Son of Ether, it's entirely possible that old and outdated concepts such as Muscle Memory are in fact <i>literally true. </i>And the Etherite <i>is not wrong. </i>To a shaman, granting aptitude in a task probably involves the spirits rather than biology; and while that shouldn't change what Spheres are used, it most definitely <i>does </i>undermine relying too heavily on science to determine which Spheres are used. The Akashayana would likely argue against body/mind duality, even as they use Life and Mind to govern distinct phenomena. <br /> <br /> What matters here is whether Abilities reside in a Mind Pattern, a Life Pattern, or some conflation of the two; that is, which Sphere should govern them. What do the <b>Mage</b> books say in that regard? If they don't say anything on the subject, then the Storyteller is on his own.<br /> <br /> Real-world neurobiology does <i>not</i> necessarily translate into <b>Mage</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-27T18:48:36-07:00","id":1544872,"title":"","content":"I would argue it's a tad more complicated because the lack of an explicit statement from the books on &quot;Abilities are governed by [Sphere]&quot; there can still be things the book says that can direct interpretations. Backgrounds that provide dots in Abilities provide some level of indication; though I would argue that they don't result in one Sphere being the &quot;Ability&quot; Sphere as Dream implies Mind, Hypercram implies Life/Mind, and Totem adds Spirit to the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T00:32:16-07:00","id":1544876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544871#post1544871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So\u2026 I find it interesting that people are arguing about specifics of human biology in the context of a game where anything too specific is arguably a factor of one's worldview rather than an objective truth.<br /> <br /> Forget about the specific details about the human nervous system. That's a Progenitors thing. To a Son of Ether, it's entirely possible that old and outdated concepts such as Muscle Memory are in fact <i>literally true. </i>And the Etherite <i>is not wrong. </i>To a shaman, granting aptitude in a task probably involves the spirits rather than biology; and while that shouldn't change what Spheres are used, it most definitely <i>does </i>undermine relying too heavily on science to determine which Spheres are used. The Akashayana would likely argue against body/mind duality, even as they use Life and Mind to govern distinct phenomena.<br /> <br /> What matters here is whether Abilities reside in a Mind Pattern, a Life Pattern, or some conflation of the two; that is, which Sphere should govern them. What do the <b>Mage</b> books say in that regard? If they don't say anything on the subject, then the Storyteller is on his own.<br /> <br /> Real-world neurobiology does <i>not</i> necessarily translate into <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isnt this the same argument as &quot;Psionic should need mind for everything&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T00:53:05-07:00","id":1544877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544870#post1544870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Seems pretty clear that I'm right, but you don't like that M20 phrased things differently from older editions. I'm not mistaken for using the wording of the most current edition of the game.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have been pretty patient towards you up to now, despite your impertinence. But the patience now is over.<br /> <br /> No, you're not right, you're absolutely, shamelessly wrong, and still remains incapable to realize it despite me showing you in detail how wrong you are. You just want to win the argument, no matter the cost, and I have no patience for intellectual dishonesty. I've shown the proof from M20 itself, but don't worry, I'll show you more. I have time to keep making a fool of yourself, it seems you do enjoy that, and as it seems, I'm not the first one that you've done that, it seems to be an habit of yours.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 20th books were largely written from the default that they were for existing fans, not new ones. That's why they're Anniversary editions that focused on being omnibus collections more than being proper new editions that advanced the game forward in design (though C20 and Wr20 got more leeway since neither of those games got a Revised edition). </div> </div> </div>I know that. The 20th anniversary editions were a compilation of the previous ones. Which is therefore laughable for you to say that every single previous editions bar none said exactly what I'm saying practically verbatim, and yet they should be discarded because of YOUR personal distorted misinterpretation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> M20 was also headed by the most prolific Mage: the Ascension developer by a huge margin. Brucato's style might be... annoying... but he's basically the only real authority on how Mage is &quot;supposed&quot; to be, considering he wrote half of 1e, headed all of 2e and Sorcerer's Crusade, and then came back to head M20 as well. If it's between some Internet rando and Brucato, Brucato's words win. </div> </div> </div>Oh, don't worry pal, I'll have some Brucato's words for you. Words who are absolutely more meaningful than your internet (dumb and ignorant) rando words. Just give me some time and I'll shove it down your throat the 1st and 2nd editions saying EXACTLY THE SAME. It's late and I'm going to bad; down bellow will be the Revised edition to end your nonsense, but don't worry, if you still keeps annoying me, I'll shove it down to you the first 2 editions too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been playing Mage for 28 years. Shove it. </div> </div> </div>And in this 28 years you didn't manage to learn anything? Damn, it truly seems some people never learn. I know people that can understand the game better than you the very first time they play. That's embarrassing actually.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And every edition established levels of possession; with variation in what you can do with each, how the target can resist, and so on. </div> </div> </div>And that has nothing to do with the argument, but nice strawman. You seem to be good at that.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, that includes connecting your mind into another person's body to the point where you can ride it around like your own body. </div> </div> </div>That's only in your moronic interpretation. Nowhere in the text does it say that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Previous editions didn't come with that caveat, but made it clear that trying to control motor actions with Mind 4 was obviously uncoordinated compared to simply issuing commands and letting the target enact the orders. Phrases like, &quot;cause an arm to twitch,&quot; are not full possession of the target's body's motor systems. </div> </div> </div>And here is where your 28 years of veterancy really &quot;shines&quot;. You're just simply taking stuff out of your ass and accepting it as truth. Maybe you've been houseruling that nonsense for so long that you ended up believing your own lie.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, that's a different amount of successes for the difference between doing something temporary vs. something permanent. </div> </div> </div>No, that's inhabiting another body rather than controlling it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And now I understand that you're arguing in complete bad faith because you only care about promoting your opinions, truth, reality, and the text of the game be damned. </div> </div> </div>Cute. Sadly I was mistaken. No, you're not arguing in good faith. You're just a spoiled child demanding to be right. I regreat treating you as an honest debater. I take that back.<br /> <br /> So now, to finally shut your nonsense up:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Ascension Revised, page 178</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Possession</b> - <i>One of the more fearsome Effects possible for Adepts of Mind, Possession allows a mage to exert direct control over the subject's thoughts. If the mage succeeds in besting the subject's Willpower, he can control the target's actions directly, either taking over the subject completely or just influencing specific, desired parts of the mind.<br /> When the mage takes total possession of a target, the victim's thoughts become overlaid with the mage's. <u>The mage need only think the appropriate actions, and the victim performs them naturally</u>, often oblivious to the invading mage. <u>The mage can direct the subject's body easily</u> (to the subject's normal limits, of course) and dig through memories or surface thoughts as with *Probe Thoughts*. The subject will even remember all of his thoughts as his own; his entire mind is subsumed by the mage's power.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>The text continues about &quot;partial possessions&quot; and how that can be used to &quot;move a body part&quot;. Go ahead, open your old book and read it, I already gave you even the page for it and even underlined the relevant parts so you can't miss. So please, cut the BS.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T01:02:21-07:00","id":1544878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544871#post1544871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So\u2026 I find it interesting that people are arguing about specifics of human biology in the context of a game where anything too specific is arguably a factor of one's worldview rather than an objective truth.<br /> <br /> Forget about the specific details about the human nervous system. That's a Progenitors thing. To a Son of Ether, it's entirely possible that old and outdated concepts such as Muscle Memory are in fact <i>literally true. </i>And the Etherite <i>is not wrong. </i>To a shaman, granting aptitude in a task probably involves the spirits rather than biology; and while that shouldn't change what Spheres are used, it most definitely <i>does </i>undermine relying too heavily on science to determine which Spheres are used. The Akashayana would likely argue against body/mind duality, even as they use Life and Mind to govern distinct phenomena.<br /> <br /> What matters here is whether Abilities reside in a Mind Pattern, a Life Pattern, or some conflation of the two; that is, which Sphere should govern them. What do the <b>Mage</b> books say in that regard? If they don't say anything on the subject, then the Storyteller is on his own.<br /> <br /> Real-world neurobiology does <i>not</i> necessarily translate into <b>Mage</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not actually the point DataWeaver. I'm not arguing &quot;science&quot; IN GAME, I'm using real life scientific knowledge as a way to facilitate communication. It's like explaining Entropy using the Mathematical Chaos Theory, Quantum Physics and the Uncertainty Principle. We are not implying that Entropy requires those to function, it's just easier to explain that Sphere using that language.<br /> <br /> Much like it is much easier to explain Spirit by using mystic terms rather than trying to convey it's concepts using some technobabble &quot;antropic-field-theory&quot; for someone that is a first timer in the game. &quot;Yes, you cross the barrier between the worlds and enter the Penumbra&quot; rather than &quot;you change phases between dimensions&quot;. Then, later on, after these concepts are understood, then you explain &quot;Dimensional Science&quot;.<br /> <br /> So, the &quot;scientific language&quot; is just a tool of understanding, not a statement of the underlying truth of the game world. AKA &quot;the Mind Sphere operates anything of the nervous system that isn't an automatic system&quot;, but that says nothing about how the Hermetics view the Mind Sphere (which is probably under the framework of dualism).<br /> <br /> In other words, that language can help elucidate the game mechanics, but it says nothing about metaphysics of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T01:24:35-07:00","id":1544879,"title":"","content":"Oh yes, I've almost forgotten:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544870#post1544870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get why you don't like the change ,but the did put most of those effects in the common effects chart instead of clustering them with the Spheres. That's where the &quot;compel sleepiness&quot; vs. &quot;put the target to sleep immediately&quot; example I used came from.</div> </div> </div> </div>Therefore, to finish your public humiliation and end either your ignorance or your dishonesty (or both):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mage the Ascension 20th anniversary, page 508, under the session of Body Magic</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sleep Spell:<br /> Mind 2 (suggest sleep);<br /> or Mind 4, Life 3, or both<br /> (compel instant slumber)</div> </div> </div> </div>My dear, you truly need to improve your reading skills. Even I that don't have English as my native language understood perfectly. Mind 2 suggests sleep BECAUSE MIND 2 <b>CANNOT DIRECTLY CONTROL A MIND</b>.<br /> But Mind 4 can! Which is why <u>you CAN compel instant slumber with EITHER Mind 4 OR Life 3 (or both) </u>- <b>BECAUSE MIND 4 CAN DIRECTLY CONTROL MINDS</b>.<br /> <br /> You clearly shouldn't pull things out of memory without being sure of what you're speaking, our memory is not infallible. Unlike you thou, I knew what I was talking about, and also unlike you, I can at any moment resort to the source material to prove me right.<br /> <br /> So yes, you definitely can put a sleep Spell on someone - with Mind 4. Mind 2 only suggests, because that's what Mind 2 does. Mind 2 only suggests, it CANNOT COMPEL. Only Mind 4 can.<br /> <br /> So, I hope this puts to rest all the rest of your nonsense. Motor actions are definitely controlled by the mind, they CAN be controlled by the Mind Sphere and this is absolutely not only evident but explicitly stated all over ALL of the editions, therefore there's nothing else to be discussed here.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T02:38:13-07:00","id":1544881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544876#post1544876\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Isnt this the same argument as &quot;Psionic should need mind for everything&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>No. I'm arguing that the choice of Spheres is usually <i>not</i> defined by form, but by function. Specifically, the shamans who invoke spirits for competence would still use either Mind or Mind and Life for the purpose, not Spirit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-28T13:00:12-07:00","id":1544909,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#c0392b\"><b>Things are getting too heated here. Ease off of personal attacks and refresh yourselves on the <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\">forum rules</a>. Warnings have been issued. </b></span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/They<br /> Moderator<br /> Line Developer: <b><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4261/Onyx-Path-Publishing/subcategory/8329_24824/Scarred-Lands-new\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","name":"TravisLegge","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25411_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"227"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-10-30T05:38:05-07:00","id":1545045,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1544449-abilities?p=1544881#post1544881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No. I'm arguing that the choice of Spheres is usually <i>not</i> defined by form, but by function. Specifically, the shamans who invoke spirits for competence would still use either Mind or Mind and Life for the purpose, not Spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, this is important. Which is why I reaffirm that downloading abilities, whatever the kind, is a purely Mind only effect (except the other variations I posted, like copy it into a physical medium - pendrives, crystals - or invoking the ability from the Cosmos with Entropy 5). I believe I made my case with concrete examples from across editions, including M20, that despite mind/body dualism, the motor functions of the body are, obviously, controlled by the mind, thus it is eligible towards being kept under the Mind Sphere.<br /> <br /> Also consider that, in case you do allow this, a commerce of &quot;abilities brain-chips&quot; (or crystals, stone tablets whatever) would probably be a thing too, particularly because Entropy Masters would be the only ones capable at trading Legendary Abilities (6+ lvls on abilities - unless you manage to find a Methuselah vampire around willing to lend some of his capabilities, which is highly unlikely)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28035-magus-maximus","name":"Magus Maximus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}